# Godot per-machine caches
.godot/
*.import
# ...except the sky plates. Their import settings are not incidental: with
# mipmaps off, the equirect pole minifies 18-57x, the samplers' own
# filter_linear_mipmap hint has nothing to filter with, and the textureLod
# call that computes the pole's mip level silently returns level 0. The
# setting has to travel with the repo or the zenith fix half-reverts on any
# fresh checkout. Committing .import is standard Godot practice anyway.
!game/assets/building/textures/sky/orison_queens_*_half_dome_4k.png.import
# ...and the 101 textures MatLib loads at runtime, force-tracked for the same
# reason. Godot only re-imports a texture with mipmaps once the EDITOR sees it
# on a 3D material, and MatLib binds these by load() at runtime, so the editor
# never sees them: on a fresh checkout Godot regenerates their .import with
# mipmaps off and the grazing-angle shimmer comes straight back. Kept by
# `git add -f`; see TASKS.md MP and art/tools/fix_runtime_texture_imports.py.
# Textures Godot EXTRACTS from the piano truck glb at import time. The glb
# embeds its four images in bufferViews (uri=None, checked); these loose
# copies are regenerated by any fresh --import, and three of the seven are
# already stale extracts of an image set the current glb no longer carries.
# Derived, not source — the glb is the deliverable.
game/assets/vehicles/*_T_*.png

*.blend1
__pycache__/
*.pyc
art/textures/_export/

# Screen recordings land in the repo root while working. They are capture
# of the work, not the work, and they are large.
Recording*.mp4
*.mp4

# Export output. The APK is ~140 MB and is rebuilt from source in a minute.
build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.idsig

# Scratch render output. Screenshot passes write comparison sets here
# while iterating; the keepers live in game/docs/screenshots.
tmp/

# Meshy animation exports. Every animation ships a complete copy of the
# character - same 266k-triangle skin, same four 2K maps - with one clip
# attached, so eleven files for one character is ~900 MB of which ~890 MB is
# the same mesh over and over. merge_meshy_animations.py folds them into a
# single ~11 MB rigged glTF in game/assets, and THAT is the deliverable.
# Re-download from Meshy if the raw exports are ever needed again.
# The whole directory, zips included — the old `*/` pattern ignored the
# extracted folders but let 400 MB source zips into a commit, which
# GitHub's pre-receive hook then declined for a full day of failed
# pushes. Masters are re-downloadable; nothing here ships.
art/blender/meshy/

# Baked per-wall finish sources. build_wall_finish_textures.py is
# deterministic (wall coordinates + id seed everything), so these 166 MB
# of PNGs are pure build artifacts; the copies the Blender export ships
# into game/assets/building are the deliverable.
art/textures/wall_finishes/

# Broadcast build intermediates. build_broadcast.py writes ~110 short mp4s
# beside the reel while assembling it; the .ogv is the deliverable.
game/assets/video/_broadcast_work/

# Raw audio source libraries. The game loads the processed files beside
# them; the masters (marked .gdignore by their own author) are ~950 MB of
# .wav/.flac that would triple the repository. soundbits/ is the untouched
# vendor library the picks were made from.
game/assets/audio/soundbits/
game/assets/audio/freesound/source/
game/assets/audio/music/source/
game/assets/audio/voice/source/

# local engine binaries, never committed
Godot_v*.exe
chunk_push.log
push_result.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Python projects folder (moved in 2026-08-07), and the things that
# travelled with it that must never enter history.
#
# Nothing under it is tracked yet on purpose: where these live, and
# whether the folder keeps a name with a space in it, is an open
# decision. These rules cover the parts that are junk under ANY layout.

# Vendored dependency dump. 84 MB, reinstallable, and the single largest
# thing that arrived with the move.
_tmp_deps/

# Test-runner cache, same class of thing as __pycache__ above.
.pytest_cache/

# Android signing material. A committed keystore is a key somebody else
# can sign your releases with; there is no undo once it is pushed, and
# rotating it orphans every install of the app. None exist in the tree
# today and none ever should.
*.keystore
*.jks
key.properties

# Android packaging intermediates and the icon source they are cut from.
# The APKs themselves are already covered by *.apk above; this is the
# rest of the build directory that produces them.
**/android/build/
icon_master.png

# Standalone packaging for the cartridge games, per the standing rule:
# their Android wrappers are how the user ships them as separate titles
# and have nothing to do with this repo. The whole android/ tree for
# Shattered; for VelvetMaze the same files sit loose at the app root
# instead of under android/, so they need naming individually.
phoneos/apps/*/android/
phoneos/apps/*/AndroidManifest.xml
phoneos/apps/*/java/
phoneos/apps/*/res/
# Local fingerprints for the incremental material ingester. Source mtimes are
# intentionally machine-local; generated texture outputs remain versioned.
art/textures/ai_materials/.ingest_state.json
